\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Band-by-band cost of the molecular-line exclusion. Union: unique sky frequency searched in the band. Masked: the part of it inside a $\pm 50$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ stellar-frame tube around a catalogued transition of one of the masked species. Left: what a technosignature search can still occupy. The mask is excluded search space and not a veto (\S  \ref  {sec:linecost}); the loss is concentrated in Band\nobreakspace  {}6, where CO\,$2\to 1$ sits.}}{19}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
